            {
                "Synonym": "Neonatal-onset cytopenia-autoinflammation-rash episodes of hemophagocytic lymphohistiocytosis syndrome"
            }
        ],
        "TextSection": {
            "TextSectionType": "Definition",
            "Contents": "A rare unclassified autoinflammatory syndrome characterized by neonatal onset pancytopenia type&nbsp;I interferon-dependent multisystemic autoinflammation painful rash with variable frequencies and hemophagocytic lymphohistiocytosis. Failure to thrive fever gastrointestinal/upper respiratory tract infections enterocolitis hepatosplenomegaly myelofibrosis and neurodevelopmental delay are other common clinical features. Facial dysmorphism including macrocephaly mild frontal bossing sparse hair mild hypertelorism depressed nasal bridge can be present."
        },
